// native-gaps-cleanup Task 8: the composition-ordering failure mode --
// `var r: SomeXRec` checks clean (the checker's declaration pass is
// two-phase, order-independent), but SomeXRec's own `extern record`
// declares AFTER the func that uses it, and lowering processes top-level
// decls in ONE sequential pass. Before this fix, lowType's TyXRec arm
// (lower.cla) called irXRecSize(irFindRecordLayoutByName(...)) with a -1
// (SomeXRec's irRecords entry not appended yet), and ir.cla's
// irRecordLayoutFieldsHead panicked on irRecords[-1] ("runtime error:
// list index out of range", exit 3). Now diagnoses instead.
//
// The diagnostic is emitted TWICE at the same position: lowering resolves
// a body-top local's declared type twice for two independent purposes
// (lowCollectScopeExitCandidates's ARC prepass, then the var-decl
// statement's own lowering) -- a pre-existing double-resolution this task
// doesn't touch (out of scope: harmless duplicate report of the same real
// error, not a second bug).
func f() {
    var r: SomeXRec
}

extern record SomeXRec {
    v: word
}
